      "locator": "Scientific abstract; PLOS PDF page 1, visually checked",
      "section_type": "Scientific abstract",
      "exact_contiguous_span": true,
      "source_identity_verified": true,
      "native_verdict": "VERIFIED",
      "inspection_limits": "Ostrowski et al. 2008, PMID:19067487; scientific abstract, publisher PDF page 1, contiguous span visually checked. Mixtures with AX4-GFP and natural-isolate dye controls support partial sorting during aggregation, not complete clonal exclusion. The measured endpoint is variation in fluorescent spore proportions among fruiting bodies; genetic distance uses 12 microsatellite loci, not genome-wide identity. Main text and all four figures were inspected; Figure 1 is hypothetical. Supplementary Tables S1 and S2 were read by text extraction. Main Methods names QS45, absent from the retrieved S1 strain table; no strain alias is inferred. Kin-selected benefit is an interpretation, not a measured fitness endpoint here. Natural provenance of every laboratory derivative and a molecular recognition mechanism remain unresolved. Native abstract verifier: VERIFIED."
    },
    {
      "reference": "DOI:10.1073/pnas.1512671112",
      "pmid": "26438858",
      "snippet": "Some swarms did merge, and most interestingly, this behavior was only seen in the most highly related strain pairs.",
      "words": 19,
      "source": {
        "path": "/tmp/traitmech-kin-source-status-20261013/stefanic2015-med.response",
