        "accessed_at": "2026-10-13T08:35:55.400546+00:00"
      },
      "locator": "Scientific abstract; EXT_ID:26438858 AND SRC:MED",
      "section_type": "Scientific abstract",
      "exact_contiguous_span": true,
      "source_identity_verified": true,
      "native_verdict": "VERIFIED",
      "inspection_limits": "Stefanic et al. 2015, PMID:26438858, PMC4653157; directly retrieved scientific abstract from Europe PMC with the namespace-qualified query EXT_ID:26438858 AND SRC:MED. Title, PMID and DOI were checked together. The authors define a conspecific scope and report relatedness-associated swarm merging versus boundary formation among sympatric Bacillus subtilis isolates. The separately reported root-colonization outcome is not a direct killing measurement. Full text, figures and supplements were inaccessible and are not claimed as inspected; indexed search passages were not used as excerpts or quantitative evidence. Native abstract verifier: VERIFIED. Linked PMID:26512099 is commentary, not a correction or experimental replication."
    },
    {
      "reference": "DOI:10.1128/mBio.00723-17",
      "pmid": "28679746",
      "snippet": "The effects of kin discrimination extend to nearby species, as the other subtilis clade species were treated with the same antagonism as nonkin.",
      "words": 23,
      "source": {
        "path": "/tmp/traitmech-kin-discrimination-canary-20261013/lyons2017-xml.response",
        "url": "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5573675/fullTextXML",
        "sha256": "340c599e88bd2162637ebe5744c8b882d49ff1ba234fefa26255872517621ff1",
        "accessed_at": "2026-10-13T08:25:43.849685+00:00"
      },
      "locator": "Scientific abstract, not IMPORTANCE; PMC5573675.1 PDF page 1, visually checked",
      "section_type": "Scientific abstract",
      "exact_contiguous_span": true,
      "source_identity_verified": true,
      "native_verdict": "VERIFIED",
      "inspection_limits": "Lyons and Kolter 2017, PMID:28679746, PMC5573675; scientific abstract, NLM version 1 PDF page 1 and JATS article-meta abstract without abstract-type. This is not the separate IMPORTANCE summary. Introduction distinguishes preferential kin association from nonkin exclusion and supports the definition's two modes; the paper's own experiments support the nearby-species extension. The comparison concerns interactions with B. subtilis NCIB3610: nearby species can be antagonized, while more distant lineages show varied outcomes. This is not a universal monotonic relation between distance and antagonism. Relatedness uses type-strain 16S, not whole-genome identity of every isolate. Swarm, biofilm and halo assays differ in medium and endpoint. Figure 2A and 2C assign WNC032 to different species; Data Set S1 identifies it as B. megaterium. No silent panel correction or taxon anchor is inferred. Actual Figures 2 and 4 and selected spreadsheet rows/totals were inspected, not all figures or raw assays. Native abstract verifier: VERIFIED. Shares an investigator with 2015; not an independent-laboratory replication."
    }
  ],
